<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Fix16: Star Wars : The Force Standalone (lee.theforce.standalone, workshop 3557220601) has one
       backstory whose description references a grammar symbol that does not exist:
         1.6/Defs/BackstoryDef/BackstoryDef_ForceSensitive.xml:113  defName Force_SithSlave
         "Once a slave on [PAWN_planetOfOrigin], ..."
       Verified: PAWN_planetOfOrigin is not a vanilla symbol, and nothing in the entire load order
       supplies it - not one XML file outside this backstory, and not one assembly (checked every
       DLL in the workshop folder for the string). It is an author oversight, not a missing
       dependency, so no mod can ever resolve it ->
         "Grammar unresolvable. Root 'r_root'  ...  PAWN_planetOfOrigin -> UNRESOLVABLE"
       When one symbol fails the whole RULE fails, so the entire description renders as nothing.
       That makes this cosmetic but total: the backstory has no readable description anywhere it is
       shown, not just in Character Editor (Character Editor merely surfaced it by calling
       BackstoryDef.FullDescriptionFor on every backstory to build its browser list).
       Replace the symbol with static prose. "a backwater world" keeps the sentence grammatical and
       biome/faction-neutral, since there is no pawn data to derive a real planet name from - the
       symbol never had a source to begin with. All other symbols in the line resolve fine and are
       left untouched. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>/Defs/BackstoryDef[defName="Force_SithSlave"]/description</xpath>
    <value>
      <description>Once a slave on a backwater world, [PAWN_nameDef]'s suffering forged an unbreakable will. When a Sith sensed [PAWN_possessive] rage, [PAWN_pronoun] was taken—not freed—to be honed into a weapon of the dark side.</description>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
